  "final_message": "I wrote `answer.json` with four functions in `billing/subscriptions.py` that emit `subscription.updated` in their own code:\n\n- **`subscriptions.transition`**: it emits `subscription.updated` for every status change except a move to `canceled`, which emits `subscription.canceled` instead.\n- **`subscriptions.change_items`**: it emits the event when a subscription's items change.\n- **`subscriptions.cancel`**: it emits the event when cancellation is scheduled for period end. A cancel that takes effect immediately goes through `transition` instead.\n- **`subscriptions.reactivate`**: it emits the event when a scheduled cancellation is undone.\n\n`pause`, `resume` and `dunning.record_failure` only reach the event by calling `transition`, so I left them out. I found no other `subscription.updated` emits in the package. I read the code but didn't run the tests.",
